•fauthorxApub:sha2-256:ks7g2ycpdnhjdtsn3sfoiqoh2tazwtiwr2emxut3ugourttnnbkadbodyßeclassharchivalgcontentxspubrules 0.49.0 was released on 2026-11-24 from commit b555eec31a80744bed361c950cefe26c0bf4e624 with these changes.ddata¢gcolumnsÇ°dnamehcategory°dnamefchangedrowsÜÇefixedxÒA Python package's sonar job now also gives SonarQube Cloud the JavaScript coverage in a lcov.info report, as a service's does, so a Python package with JavaScript code no longer needs a sonar-args path into the runner's temporary directory.Çgchangedyâpub* packages are pinned by their PyPI names: requirements-pubrules.txt requires `pubtestrules>=0.4.0` and `pubrules==X`, tests/requirements.txt pins `pubtestrules==X` (sync pins by name the release a wheel pin of pubrules 0.48.0 and before names, raised to the floor), the lock holds each with every published hash, and `pubrules lock` refuses any package named pubtest (PyPI's other project)ÇgchangedxÎ./pubrules runs `uvx --from pubrules==X` from PyPI; with a wheel mirror (mirror.wheels) it still fetches pubrules' release wheel, from GitHub or else the mirror, checked against the sha256 tests/requirements.lock pins for `pubrules==X`Çeaddedxﬁthe nightly moves each pub* package a requirements file pins by name (`pubtestrules==X` among them) to its newest release on PyPI with a file not yanked, or on the PyPI mirror where pubrules.json names one, and locks againÇeaddedy The sonar job of a generated ci block (job-sonar.yml) no longer lets SonarQube Cloud being down block a pull request or a deploy: its scan only uploads, and a gate step then asks SonarQube Cloud for the result. A failed or refused quality gate still fails the job, but when SonarQube Cloud gives no answer after three tries, the job passes with a warning and a note in its summary if the pull request carries the label sonar-down (for a push to main, the pull request merged into it). The main run's sonar job gets pull-requests: read for that.ÇeaddedyThe Python standard: a Python package or a service whose ci block's with gives a lint command ("lint": "make lint") gets a lint job (job-python-lint.yml, ci / lint) that runs setup and then that command, with Ruff's findings shown on the pull request. sync then manages pubrules-ruff.toml, the shared Ruff rules (Ruff's defaults with bugbear, simplify, pyupgrade, isort and pylint's size limits, line length 120, Ruff's formatter), and pins ruff 0.17.6 beside it in tests/requirements-pubrules.txt; sync --check fails until pyproject.toml's [tool.ruff] extends pubrules-ruff.toml, while it sets line-length, select, ignore or extend-ignore over it, and until tests/requirements.lock pins that Ruff. pubrules-python.mk gains make lint (ruff check, then ruff format --check) and make fmt.gdependsÅxApub:sha2-256:b6yzbl6hucsncujwfis7bqn5wjofwv7z6y75nhrs6ie3ud6crauahevidenceÅ§dkindhexternalcrefhpubruleshrevisionx(b555eec31a80744bed361c950cefe26c0bf4e624drolefsourcedlangbenescope¢jconditionsÄfdomainx)the published release v0.49.0 of pubrulesgcreatedt2026-11-24T00:00:00Zcpuba1dtypekclaim.prose